    <section class="tour" id="tour">
      <header class="intro">
        <h2>Everything agents need from you, <em>in one place</em></h2>
        <p>Choose a feature to try it in the window above, or explore the details below.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="tour-grid">
        <ol class="tour-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Features">
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="sessions" aria-selected="true"><b>Sessions</b><span>Chat or terminal, grouped by project and worktree.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="inbox"><b>Needs you</b><span>The inbox lists every agent waiting on an answer.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="review"><b>Review</b><span>Diffs, commits and the pull request, beside the session.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="worktrees"><b>Worktrees</b><span>A branch, a folder and an agent in one step.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="board"><b>Board</b><span>Tickets across projects. Start one and it gets a worktree.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="automations"><b>Automations</b><span>Prompts that run on a schedule, even with the app closed.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="delegated"><b>Delegated work</b><span>A chat hands work to other agents and waits for results.</span></button></li>
          <li><button role="tab" data-go="hosts"><b>Other machines</b><span>Add a Mac, Linux or Windows host over SSH.</span></button></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="tour-cards">
          <article class="card status-card">
            <h3>Status you can trust</h3>
            <p>Claude Code and Codex report their own state from a terminal. Every agent reports it from a chat.</p>
            <ul class="lifecycle" aria-label="Session statuses">
              <li class="s-working"><i class="spin"></i>Working</li>
              <li class="s-needs"><i></i>Needs you</li>
              <li class="s-done"><i></i>Done</li>
              <li class="s-failed"><i></i>Failed</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Sessions that survive</h3>
            <p>A daemon, pocketd, owns every terminal. Close the window and your agents keep running.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Native, not a browser</h3>
            <p>The desktop app is Rust on GPUI. A Changes list with 1,137 files draws in about 3 ms.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="native" id="native">
      <div class="native-inner">
        <div class="intro">
          <h2>Rust on the GPU,<br><em>native all the way down</em></h2>
          <p>The window is Rust on GPUI, drawn on the GPU like a game. A small Go daemon runs your terminals and agents, and keeps them running when the window closes. There's no bundled Chromium and no Node runtime.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="native-grid">
          <div class="native-stack">
            <div class="layer">
              <i data-icon="sidebar"></i>
              <div><b>The window</b><span>Rust · GPUI · drawn on the GPU</span></div>
              <code>pocket-desktop</code>
            </div>
            <div class="layer">
              <i data-icon="server"></i>
              <div><b>The daemon</b><span>Go · terminals, sessions, Board, automations</span></div>
              <code>pocketd</code>
            </div>
            <div class="layer">
              <i data-icon="terminal"></i>
              <div><b>Your agents</b><span>The CLIs you already installed</span></div>
              <code>claude, codex, …</code>
            </div>
            <div class="layer gone" aria-label="Not in Anywhere: Chromium and Node.js">
              <i data-icon="x"></i>
              <div><b>Chromium + Node.js</b><span>Not in the box</span></div>
            </div>
            <p class="native-note">The only web view is the built-in browser, for pages you open in it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="native-stats">
            <div class="metric">
              <b>3<small>ms</small></b>
              <p>One frame of a Changes list with 1,137 files</p>
              <span class="meter" style="--v: 0.36" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
              <span class="budget">of an 8.3 ms frame at 120 Hz</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <b>3.8<small>ms</small></b>
              <p>One frame while scrolling a chat of 1,200 items</p>
              <span class="meter" style="--v: 0.46" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
              <span class="budget">of an 8.3 ms frame at 120 Hz</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <b>~100<small>ms</small></b>
              <p>From clicking a file to seeing its diff</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

