    <section class="faq" id="faq">
      <header class="intro">
        <h2>Questions</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="faq-grid">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>What is Anywhere?</h3>
            <p>A native desktop app for watching and driving many coding agents in one window. The window is Rust on GPUI, and a small Go daemon runs the agents. It runs on macOS 13 or later, with a build for Linux too. Windows machines can be remote hosts over SSH.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Which coding agents does it support?</h3>
            <p>Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Grok Build, OpenCode, Pi, omp, fx, Hermes Agent and Antigravity. Anywhere runs the CLIs you already installed and signed in to.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Can I run multiple Claude Code or Codex agents at once?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Sessions are grouped by project and git worktree. Each one is Working, Needs you, Done, Failed or Idle, and Needs you, Failed and Done show in the sidebar, the inbox, the Dock badge and notifications.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Do sessions keep running if I close the window?</h3>
            <p>Yes. The daemon, pocketd, owns the terminals, so agents keep running. Automations also run while the desktop app is closed.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Can I answer an agent from my phone?</h3>
            <p>Coming soon. A native SwiftUI app for iPhone and iPad pairs with your Mac over Tailscale, with push notifications and Live Activities.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Is Anywhere free and open source?</h3>
            <p>Yes. It is MIT licensed, with no account, no cloud tier and no premium tier. The source is at <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere">github.com/mingo023/anywhere</a>.</p>
          </article>
      </div>
